  "body": "Part of #1448.\n\nThe first slice of #1448 (PR for branch `issue/1448-start-exit-points`) adds a user-set **start point** on closed 2D Contour rings only (`links.approach.start_point`, settable through `EditOperationParams`, the project file and MCP `edit_operation`). Everything below is refused by name today and is owed:\n\n1. **Exit points** - a user-set point where the cut leaves the ring (lead-out placed there), with the same \"a pick is a wish, refused by name if the lead law cannot hold it\" rule.\n2. **Viewport pick + property row** - click on the wall in the viewport to set or clear the start/exit point, and an X/Y row on the Lead in / Lead out tab; structural tests updated, before/after screenshots in the PR.\n3. **Start point with tabs** - re-measure the tab windows from the picked start.\n4. **Start point with control / wear compensation** - the seam is the compensation law's (engage/cancel on a straight run); prove the picked seam against it.\n5. **Open chains** - a pick choosing which end (or a point along the run) the cut starts from.\n6. **Tilted (3+2) contours** - the pick in the tilted frame.\n7. **Other operations** - entry placement for Pocket / Adaptive (where the helix or ramp descends) and the 3D finishing strategies; each kind needs its own refusal law and may become its own issue.\n\nDone means: each item above is either shipped with a pinning test (refusals by name where the lead or entry law cannot hold the pick) or split into its own issue linked here.\n",
